                        <div class="report-prose market-size-prose"><p>The US Mini PC Market was valued at USD 3.5 billion in 2024 and is projected to reach USD 8.2 billion by 2034, registering a CAGR of 8.9%. This growth trajectory is underpinned by the increasing demand for compact computing solutions that offer high performance while occupying minimal space. The proliferation of remote work and online education has significantly boosted the adoption of mini PCs, as they provide an efficient alternative to traditional desktop computers. According to industry reports, the demand for mini PCs in educational institutions has surged, with a notable increase in procurement for both classroom and administrative use. Furthermore, the gaming sector is witnessing a shift towards miniaturized systems that deliver powerful performance without the bulk, catering to gamers who prioritize portability and space efficiency.</p>
<p>The market is also benefiting from advancements in technology, including the integration of powerful processors and enhanced graphics capabilities in smaller form factors. As consumers increasingly seek devices that offer versatility and mobility, mini PCs are becoming a preferred choice for various applications, including home entertainment, gaming, and professional use. The trend towards smart homes and IoT devices is further driving the demand for mini PCs, as these systems can serve as central hubs for managing connected devices.</p></div>
                        <div class="figure-block" id="figure1">
                            <div class="figure-label-row">
                                <span class="figure-label">Figure 1</span>
